---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import features from "../../data/features.json";
---
<SiteLayout title="Planned features — Retail POS Mobile" description="Review the planned direction for checkout, inventory, till control, offline sync, roles, and retail operations. These capabilities are not yet available in a public release." path="/features/">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Features</div><span class="eyebrow">Planned scope</span><h1>What the product is being built toward.</h1><p>These are the intended capability areas for Retail POS Mobile. They remain labelled as planned until each workflow is implemented, tested, and approved for release.</p><div class="status-line"><span class="status-pill status-planned"><span class="status-dot"></span> Planned—not released</span></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="container"><div class="notice"><span class="notice-icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span><div><strong>Availability note</strong><p>No public production build is available yet. This page is a roadmap-level description, not a feature guarantee.</p></div></div><div class="card-grid">{features.map((feature,index)=><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{String(index+1).padStart(2,"0")}</span><span class="status-pill status-planned"><span class="status-dot"></span> Planned</span><h3>{feature.title}</h3><p><strong>Intended outcome:</strong> {feature.outcome}</p><p>{feature.planned_scope}</p>{feature.id==="offline"&&<a class="text-link" href="/offline-first/">Read offline design notes <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>}</article>)}</div><div class="notice"><span class="notice-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><strong>Evidence before promotion</strong><p>A planned capability moves to “available” only after code, relevant tests, and the release build have been reviewed.</p></div></div></div></section></SiteLayout>
